# The v3 proposal: keep full post-codec fidelity, add a spatially targeted rate
# penalty instead of pulling the preprocessed clip back toward the source.
#
# Why: every run so far raised bitrate. A single scalar lambda*bpp has a dynamic
# range of about 0.010-0.012 over these QPs, so it cannot express "spend fewer
# bits here and more bits there". The masked total variation can: it penalizes
# spatial and temporal detail exactly where the frozen analyzer does not look.
# It also reaches the preprocessor as an exact analytic gradient, while lambda*bpp
# can only arrive through the frozen proxy's rate head.
#
# On 128x128 input the r3d_18 preset resizes to 128x171 and crops 112x112, so the
# analyzer only sees rows 8:120 and columns 22:106, that is 57.4% of every frame.
# The remaining 42.6% costs bits that cannot change the prediction.
#
# Weight scale: compare gradients, not loss values. At MSE 0.002 the mean absolute
# reconstruction error is about 0.045, so alpha * d(MSE)/dz is near 2*10*0.045 =
# 0.9 per pixel. A masked-TV weight of 1.0 applies comparable pressure. Sweep
# 0.25, 1, 4. The logged mask_rate itself lands near 0.05-0.15 for real video.

--preprocessor swin
--swin-qp-conditioning
--swin-qp-embed-dim 64
--max-residual 0.25

--codec h264
--codec-qps 30 35 40 45

--alpha 10
--rate-lambda 0.05

# eta = 1.0: MSE against the source is measured after the codec only. The masked
# penalty is now the term that suppresses expensive detail, so the identity pull
# of MSE(processed, source) is not needed and would fight it.
--distortion-reconstruction-weight 1.0

--ce-weight 1.0
--kd-weight 0.5
--kd-temperature 2.0
--feature-weight 0.05
--feature-layer layer4

--mask-rate-weight 1.0
--mask-rate-target output
--mask-rate-layer layer4
--mask-rate-gamma 1.0
--mask-rate-outside-weight 1.0

--optimizer adamw
--weight-decay 0.01
--lr 0.0001
--clip-grad 1.0
--checkpoint-metric task_bd_rate
